    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1357">

                <pb facs="1062" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg946"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/865.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Davis to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 587.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Guadalajara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-09-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 18, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * The Carrancista Government has
                    abrogated the edict as to the re-collection of taxes paid to the Villistas.</p>
                <p>As, according to the mining tax law, owners have until the end of October before
                    forfeiting all rights to redeem, I am advising them to take the full time before
                    paying, which they can do with safety.</p>
                <p>If the Department can give me instructions as to how to better or further advise,
                    I would feel thankful.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Will B. Davis.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
